<td id="S6.T4.2.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S6.T4.2.7.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">+39.4%</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analysis</span>: Observed slowdowns result from confounded factors. <span id="S6.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Normalized time analysis</span> (per 1000 characters) reveals parallel coordination is faster per character for 5/6 tasks (11–52% speedup when controlling for code volume). Raw slowdowns are <span id="S6.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">artifacts of code generation volume</span>—parallel produces 82–189% more code with optimizations/safety checks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>RQ2: Code Quality—Mixed Results</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mixed results</span>: Parallel excels at performance (+25%, p<math id="S6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.001, d_z=1.51) but degrades code quality (-7.7%, p<math id="S6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.001, d_z=-0.71) and accessibility (-5.6%, p<math id="S6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.001, d_z=-0.59). Architecture unchanged (p=0.158).</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Objective Metrics</span>: Static analysis (TypeScript errors, code length) on all 600 samples shows task-dependent outcomes (Table <a href="#S6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 6.3 RQ2: Code Quality—Mixed Results ‣ 6 Results and Discussion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Per-task objective metrics (Mann-Whitney U tests; ***p<math id="S6.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.001, **p<math id="S6.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.01, *p<math id="S6.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.05). Highly task-dependent: 5/6 tasks show -46% to -87% error rate reductions; Markdown Editor worsens (+24%). Code length: -12% to +189%. Critical Correlation: All tasks with highest code inflation (Pomodoro, Dashboard, Visualizer: +82–189% code) exhibit largest slowdowns (+29–39%), confounding attribution to coordination overhead alone.</figcaption>
